# <%= a.title %> — Authentication

RubyRoad inferred this provider's auth from OpenAPI `components.securitySchemes`<% if a.default_security.any? %> and the document-level `security` requirement (`<%= a.default_security.join(', ') %>`)<% end %>.

## Scheme used by the generated client

<% case a.auth_kind -%>
<% when :api_key -%>
**API key header** — every request sends `<%= a.auth_header %>: <api_key>`.

```ruby
<%= module_name %>.configure do |config|
  config.api_key = ENV.fetch("<%= module_name.upcase %>_API_KEY")
  config.environment = :sandbox # or :live
end
```
<% when :basic -%>
**HTTP Basic** — `Authorization: Basic base64(api_key:secret)`.

```ruby
<%= module_name %>.configure do |config|
  config.api_key = ENV.fetch("<%= module_name.upcase %>_API_KEY")
  config.secret  = ENV.fetch("<%= module_name.upcase %>_SECRET")
  config.environment = :sandbox
end
```
<% else -%>
**HTTP Bearer** — `Authorization: Bearer <api_key>`.

```ruby
<%= module_name %>.configure do |config|
  config.api_key = ENV.fetch("<%= module_name.upcase %>_API_KEY")
  config.environment = :sandbox # or :live
end
```
<% end -%>

