<% if a.has_idempotency -%>
## Idempotency

Write operations accept `idempotency_key:` which is sent as the `<%= a.idempotency_header %>` header. Replays with the same key return the original result instead of creating a second payment or refund.

```ruby
client.create_payment(
  amount: 2500,
  currency: "USD",
  idempotency_key: SecureRandom.uuid
)
```
<% end -%>

<% if a.has_webhooks -%>
## Webhooks (HMAC-SHA256)

Inbound events are signed with **HMAC-SHA256**. The generated verifier expects:

```
<%= a.webhook_header %>: t=<unix_timestamp>,v1=<hex_digest>
```

The signed string is `"<timestamp>.<raw_body>"` using `config.webhook_secret`.

```ruby
<%= module_name %>::Webhooks.handle(request.body.read, request.get_header("HTTP_<%= a.webhook_header.upcase.tr('-', '_') %>")) do |event|
  case event.type
<% a.webhook_events.map(&:type).uniq.each do |type| -%>
  when <%= type.inspect %>
    # ...
<% end -%>
  end
end
```

TODO: if the provider signs only the raw body (no timestamp prefix), change `Webhooks.verify!` to match their docs.
<% end -%>

